[{:seon.task/name "each-run-teaches-the-next"
  :seon.task/plan "Learn from every run automatically, without regressions, slowdown or growth (DECISIONS: every live run better than the last). Reproduction: the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's code (the task ``seon.reconcile/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded``, since finished) spent 8 turns and 59 errors without a fix; the causes were readable only by querying its branch's evaluation records: ``clojure.repl/source`` failing for platform vars, `slurp` of repository files not found, guessed namespaces. What exists: `seon.learn/waste` charges a run's wasted forms to the context producer that led to them, and the judge records it (`:seon.task/waste`, the agent's own `:seon.agent/waste`, `seon.reconcile/judge-tx`, class `:waste` in `seon.problems`). Correct, extending that and adding nothing beside it: the record answers \"what did this run lack\": its failed forms grouped by kind (an unresolved var or namespace, no source, file not found, a contract's error, a wrong arity), each with its count and one example, and the names it tried to read that its context did not show. `my.root/problems` ranks the lacks of every run on main by kind, most frequent first, one example each, so the next fix is the commonest gap across a steady stream of new real tasks (no matrix of reruns). The agent's instructions (the help page, `docs/agent.md`) name today's functions (`my.schema/register!`, `source`), each resolving. Budget: about 120 net src lines; no new namespace; nothing on the turn's hot path beyond the fold at the run's end. (`seon.turn/context-block` already takes gaps since the merge base.)"
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/a-run-records-what-it-lacked
                      seon.problems-test/lacks-are-ranked-across-runs
                      seon.ctx.wire-test/the-server-context-shows-only-new-contract-gaps}}
 {:seon.task/name "turns-to-green-report"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner's key number: turns to a good solution, from all runs (AGENTS §1). What exists: :seon.agent/turn, :seon.model-call/tokens, cache-hit-tokens and cache-miss-tokens, and :seon.task/waste are recorded; `seon.learn` has `seon.learn/waste` and `seon.learn/summary` only, and nothing reports turns to green. v1: `seon.mine` and ``my.root/turns-report`` (median and p90 per step, model and commit; ~/src/seon/src/seon/mine.clj). Correct: a new ``seon.learn/report``, one query: median and p90 turns to green per template (step), per model and per main commit; tokens and cost per green; cache-hit share; the top waste rules. It renders on its schema on the dashboard and in root's context (`:seon.render/root-context`, rendered by `seon.render.ui/root-context`)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/report-quantiles-match-recorded-runs}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-runs-waste-is-folded-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by context's duplication audit, 2026-11-14 (the owner: no duplicated effort; plan item 7), both ends read [M]. An ended run's waste is folded from its evals three ways with three 'shown' sets: seon.turn/end! (its task's own proofs and cites, stored as :seon.agent/waste), seon.learn/run (passes {}, so nothing counts as re-read), and seon.ctx.status (cites, with the needs' proofs from pulled-accumulated). The refine agent and my.root/run-losses read a summary that differs from the stored one. Change: one function answers the shown set of a task on a db, read by all three; learn/run and run-losses read the stored summary when the run ended. Deletes: the {} fold and the second shown builder. Proof: learn/run of an ended run equals its stored :seon.agent/waste."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/a-runs-waste-is-folded-once}}
 {:seon.task/name "progress-folds-each-commits-datoms"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: context; runtime reviews (the core's delta fold: state + a commit's datoms -> state'). The follow-up of seon.reconcile/an-agent-with-no-progress-by-turn-x-is-refined-and-restarted: seon.learn/progress is first a recompute per turn over the run's evals (O(evals), bounded by the cap: ~40 x 5M ticks a run); then a fold that takes each commit's own datoms (an eval's :recorded vars, the task's plan datoms) into the run's marks, O(datoms a commit wrote), health's fold its first caller. Proof: seon.learn-test/progress-folds-a-commit-at-the-cost-of-its-datoms."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/progress-folds-a-commit-at-the-cost-of-its-datoms}
  :seon.task/estimate #:seon.learn{progress {:n 20, :order :linear, :ticks 200000, :bytes 1000000}}
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.ratom/a-commit-reaches-only-the-readers-of-what-it-moved"}}]
